# Light infantry: open order, every man his own shot from behind whatever is there.
# v2 (2026-10-05): a real skirmish screen - takes the ground, harasses from cover, gives way to
# a charge and comes back, keeps out of its own smoke, presses a wavering enemy.
drill "Skirmishers"
about "Open order in front of the army: each man fires at will from cover, steps out of his own smoke, gives way before a charge and comes back, and presses an enemy that wavers."
type Marksman
dials aggression 0.35 discipline 0.35 cohesion 0.15 cover 0.95 patience 0.45 nerve 0.50

sergeant:
  when enemy charging and enemy within 35  -> fall back 20; form skirmish; find cover
  when enemy breaking or enemy broken      -> advance; form skirmish; fire at will
  when losing the exchange                 -> fall back 15; form skirmish; find cover; fire at will
  when enemy within 70                     -> hold; form skirmish; find cover; fire at will
  otherwise                                -> advance; form skirmish; find cover; fire at will

man:
  when enemy within 6                      -> bayonet
  when enemy charging and enemy within 20 and loaded -> fire; back 10
  when enemy charging and enemy within 20  -> back 12
  when in smoke and enemy beyond 20        -> step out of the smoke
  when in cover and loaded and enemy within 75 -> fire
  when on high ground and loaded and enemy within 85 -> fire
  when not in cover and enemy within 75    -> take cover within 12
  when loaded and enemy within 55          -> fire
  when not loaded                          -> reload kneeling
  # a skirmisher kneels: half the target, a steadier rest for the rifle, harder to pick out
  otherwise                                -> hold kneeling
